{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Understanding Data Resources"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear or use to talk about data resources. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about relational database management system in spoken or written texts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses information a wider range of contexts about exchanging technical information on software programming and software solutions, using appropriate grammar and vocabulary at this level.  Recognizes simple ideas on concepts on software programming, software solutions and database management."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n7le01ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Be Supposed to in Affirmative Statements"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "\"<b>Be supposed to</b>\" is used to show expectation in the past, the present, or the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Be supposed to</strong> means something is planned, arranged, or expected.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">It is important to consider what tense you want to use in order to coherently use the corresponding form of the verb to <strong>be</strong> preceding the words <strong>supposed to</strong>. Remember that this verb phrase always uses a principal verb in the infinitive form after <strong>supposed to</strong>.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If someone, for example, says you <strong>are supposed to do something</strong>, that person is trying to say that you are expected to do something in the present.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If someone, on the other hand, says that something <strong>was</strong> <strong>supposed to</strong> happen, that person is trying to say that something was expected to happen but never did.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Take a look at the following examples.</p> <p><i>We <strong>are supposed to</strong> find a good job in the IT sector.</i></p> <p><i>She <strong>was supposed to</strong> contact the managers beforehand. </i></p> <p><i>Technology <strong>is supposed to</strong> facilitate people&rsquo;s lives.</i></p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "For today's meeting, we are supposed to discuss several aspects to understand data."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We are supposed to explain that data resources of information systems are typically organized into databases and knowledge bases."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Conditional Sentences with If Clauses, First Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The <b>first conditional</b> is used to talk about situations that might happen in the future; it describes consequences which may easily come true. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "STRUCTURE</br>The <b>first conditional</b> is composed by a condition and a result."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Condition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If + Present tense +,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"will / can / may / must + verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>If  you <b>are</b> an IT expert,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>you <b>will</b> have many job opportunities.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can change the position of the clauses. Thus, your sentence can start with the clause containing the result and, then, be followed by the one explaining the condition. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If condition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"will + base verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Simple\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>I <b>will stay</b> in my current job</i>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>if my boss <b>offers</b> me a raise. \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you work in the IT sector, you will have to differentiate databases from data."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I will write a short summary with key points if you help me with the training. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Notice two things:</br></br>1. There is always a clause that contains the word \"if\".</br>2. When you change the position of the clauses, the meaning is not affected, but you need to change the punctuation as well. So, if you start your conditional sentence with the \"if\" clause, you will necessarily include a comma at the end of this clause. However, if you start your sentence by expressing the result, you won't have to include any comma at the end of this initial clause."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "infrastructure "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the basic systems and services, such as transport and power supplies, that a country or organization uses in order to work effectively "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The data resource is a separate component of this infrastructure."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le01ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "differentiate "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to show or find the difference between things "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  You will have to differentiate databases from data."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le01ob04aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "spreadsheet"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a computer program, used especially in business, that allows you to do financial calculations and plans "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Some other examples of data are MP3, video files, spreadsheets, web pages, and e-books."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le01ob04aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "summary "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a short description that provides the main facts or ideas about something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I will write a short summary with key points if you help me with the training. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le01ob04aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "belong "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to  have the appropriate qualifications to be part of a group"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Data belongs to a database."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le01ob04aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "allow"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to give someone or something permission to do something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Databases are more powerful ways to define the types of data that go into each field, reducing possible errors and allowing easier analysis."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le01ob04aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe7n7le01ob04re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">For today's meeting, we are supposed to discuss several aspects to understand data. First of all, an information system refers to the combination of users, technology, and processes to complete a specific goal. These users are supposed to utilize hardware and software, typically in a network format, to process raw data into usable information. Therefore, if companies get the latest technology without paying attention to staff training, goals will be difficult to achieve. Users, technology, and processes are supposed to work together to get a specific goal."}, {"time": "43000", "image": "enpe7n7le01ob04re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">Secondly, Data Resource is a component of information system infrastructure that represents all the data available to an organization. If organizations are automated or non-automated, they will have different needs. The data resource is a separate component of this infrastructure. However, a digital data resource is supposed to provide faster and more efficient options for managing data for companies. Data is the raw material or information with no context; for example, if you have software, you will need data to do anything useful."}, {"time": "84000", "image": "enpe7n7le01ob04re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">Some other examples of data are MP3, video files, spreadsheets, web pages, and e-books. If you look for types of data, you will identify text, number, alphanumeric text, and objects such as images or music files. If you work in the IT sector, you will have to differentiate databases from data.  Whereas data belongs to a database, databases are more powerful ways to define the types of data that go into each field, reducing possible errors and allowing easier analysis.<br/>\nFinally, as a member of the IT department, you need to analyze information about data resources; for example, we are supposed to explain that data resources of information systems are typically organized into databases and knowledge bases.   For now, I will write a short summary with key points if you help me with the training."}], "coverimg": "enpe7n7le01ob04re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n7le01ob04re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can explain the data resources in information systems. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "  I can give examples of data resources in information systems.  "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can analyze information related to data resources in information systems."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How important do you think it is for companies to train their staff in using the latest technology?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "In your own words, what is the difference between data and database?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Combining Users and Technology to Understand Data"}], "img_path": "", "id": 0}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "templ